            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "You cannot just call `.calculate_constant_result()` of a node because it's not guaranteed to succeed. `self._calculate_const()` does it correctly, but it also evaluates the whole node subtree, which should only be done once (although it doesn't hurt to repeat it).\n\nI'd start by folding the two cases here into the if-blocks above and see where that leaves us.",
            "commit_id": "6735fbfc333a6e8d9cc33c933a0de90c1695a157",
            "created_at": "2026-10-01T22:13:58Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -4775,6 +4775,10 @@ def _calculate_constant_seq(self, node, sequence_node, factor):\n                     return self.visit_BinopNode(node)\n             else:\n                 sequence_node.mult_factor = factor\n+            if sequence_node.mult_factor is None:\n+                sequence_node.calculate_constant_result()",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/cython/cython/pull/8021#discussion_r4161043900",
